commitMessage.commandInputTemplate:
Write a git commit message for the staged changes on {branch}.

Staged files:
{stagedFiles}

Staged diff:
{stagedPatch}

Format: conventional commits, `<type>(<scope>): <subject>`, imperative, subject max 50 chars, no trailing period. Add a body wrapped at 72 chars only if the change needs a "why". Add a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer if applicable.
If a GitHub issue number is linked, add a footer "Refs #<number>" using this value, and add nothing if it is empty: {linkedIssue}
Describe only what's in the diff. No emoji, no AI attribution, no Co-authored-by.
Output ONLY the commit message.

pullRequest.commandInputTemplate:
{basePrompt}

Style rules (apply on top of the above):
- Title: imperative, max 72 chars, no emoji or trailing period.
- Body sections: ## Summary (1–3 sentences), ## Changes (bullets by area), ## Testing (only what's verifiable; otherwise "Not tested"), ## Notes (only migrations, config, breaking changes, or risks; omit if none).
- If this value is a GitHub issue number, end the body with "Closes #<number>"; if it is empty, add nothing: {linkedIssue}
- If a title or description was already typed, keep its intent: {currentTitle} / {currentBody}
- Describe only what's in the diff. No filler, no AI attribution.
